# Everything the build does not need, and several things it must not have.
#
# This file is not housekeeping. Without it, `docker build` sends the whole
# working tree - including bin/, obj/ and any local secrets - into the build
# context, which is slow, invalidates the layer cache on every rebuild, and can
# bake a developer's credentials into an image.

# ── Build output ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Critically: a host bin/ or obj/ copied into the image would collide with the
# container's own restore and produce errors that look nothing like their cause.
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/out/
**/publish/
**/TestResults/
**/*.user
**/*.suo

# ── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
**/appsettings.Development.json
**/appsettings.Local.json
**/secrets.json
**/*.pfx
**/*.key
**/*.pem

# ── Source control and tooling ───────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.sln.DotSettings.user

# ── Tests ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The published image restores and builds only Marketing.API and its references.
tests/

# ── Documentation and local files ────────────────────────────────────────────
*.md
docs/
Dockerfile*
docker-compose*.yml
.dockerignore
